Package: linux-device-manager
Version: __VERSION__
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Linux Device Manager <dev@example.com>
Depends: libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.14.5), policykit-1, udev
Recommends: pciutils, usbutils, kmod, systemd
Description: View and manage hardware devices
 Linux Device Manager is a GTK4 application that enumerates devices
 from sysfs/udev, displays them in a category tree with detail tabs
 (general, advanced, driver, logs), and allows enabling/disabling
 devices through a privileged helper governed by polkit.
 .
 Bundles a trimmed JRE (jlink). Depends on the system GTK4 runtime.
Homepage: https://github.com/albilu/linux-device-manager
